msgstr ""

msgctxt "PcaEfaAnalysisOptions|"
msgid ""
"If one observation from a variable is missing, all the other variable "
"observations from the same case will still be used for the analysis. In this "
"scenario, it is not necessary to have an observation for all the variables "
"to include the case in the analysis. This option is selected by default."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "PcaEfaAnalysisOptions|"
msgid "Exclude cases listwise"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "PcaEfaAnalysisOptions|"
msgid ""
"If one observation from a variable is missing, the whole case, so all the "
"other connected variable observations, will be dismissed from the analysis. "
"In this scenario, observations for every variable are needed to include the "
"case in the analysis. "
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Confirmatory factor analysis (CFA) models observed variables (indicators) as "
"manifestations of underlying latent variables (factors). Scale and ordinal "
"variables can be assigned to factors. There is a minimum of one factor, and "
"each factor needs at least two indicators. Add a factor with the (+) button "
"and remove it with the (-) button. A factor can be renamed by changing the "
"name above its assignment box. If any ordinal variable is used, the "
"estimator defaults to DWLS and the test statistic and fit measures are "
"scaled and shifted (mean and variance adjusted, see the lavaan "
"documentation). Other possible estimators are WLS and ULS. With ordinal "
"variables it may make sense to use robust standard errors."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Specifies whether the data is raw, meaning observations in rows and "
"variables in columns, or whether the data is a variance-covariance matrix. "
"For the latter, the sample size is required."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid "Use raw data with observations as rows and variables in columns."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Use a variance-covariance matrix as input. Requires specifying the sample "
"size."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid "The number of observations the variance-covariance matrix is based on."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"The factors can in turn be indicators of a second-order factor. Any factors "
"not assigned as indicators of the second-order factor are allowed to covary "
"with each other and with the second-order factor, but not with the "
"indicators of the second-order factor."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Drag the factors that should be indicators of a second-order factor into "
"this box."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Options for the model specification: mean structure, factor correlations, "
"identification and residual covariances."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Display the means for the indicators and, in the case of multigroup CFA, the "
"means of the latent variables. To identify the model, one of the following "
"constraints needs to be chosen."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Which intercepts are fixed to zero to identify the model with a mean "
"structure."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Fix the latent intercepts (factor means) to zero. The manifest intercepts "
"are estimated freely."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Fix the manifest intercepts to zero. The latent intercepts (factor means) "
"are estimated freely."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Fix the mean of the manifest intercepts to zero, which translates to effects "
"coding. The latent intercepts (factor means) are estimated freely."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid "Set the correlations between the different latent variables to 0."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid "How the factors are given a scale. The default is marker variable."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"The factor has the same scale as its first indicator, because the factor "
"loading of that indicator is fixed to 1."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid "The factor has a fixed variance of 1."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid "The mean of the factor loadings of a factor is fixed to 1."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Allow for covariance between indicators that is not explained by their "
"respective factor, for example because the questions were phrased in a "
"similar way. Drag two variables to the right-side assignment box to let them "
"covary."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid "Pairs of indicators whose residuals are allowed to covary."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Fit the CFA model separately for each group of a grouping variable and "
"optionally constrain parameters to be equal across groups."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid "Select a categorical variable here to create CFA models for each group."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid "Select a level of constraining parameters over the different groups."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid "The different groups have the same CFA structure."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Same as configural, and the factor loadings are constrained to be equal "
"across groups."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Same as metric, and the means of the indicators (intercepts) are constrained "
"to be equal across groups."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Same as scalar, and the residual variances and residual covariances are "
"constrained to be equal across groups."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Same as strict, and the latent means, variances, and covariances are "
"constrained to be equal across groups."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Additional tables with fit measures, assumption checks, validity and "
"reliability measures, covariance matrices, modification indices and the "
"lavaan syntax."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Display the values of various fit measures: incremental fit indices (e.g., "
"CFI, TLI), information criteria (log-likelihood, AIC, BIC, SSABIC) and other "
"measures (e.g., RMSEA with 90% confidence interval, SRMR). Information "
"criteria are only available with ML-type estimators."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Determines how well the indicators are suited for factor analysis by "
"computing the proportion of common variance between them. Produces a measure "
"of sampling adequacy (MSA) for each indicator and overall; values closer to "
"1 are desired."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Tests whether the correlation matrix of the indicators is the identity "
"matrix, meaning whether the indicators are related or not. A significant "
"result means the correlation matrix is unlike the identity matrix."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Display the proportion of variance in each indicator that is explained by "
"all predictors (the factors)."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Display the average variance extracted: the amount of variance that is "
"captured by a construct in relation to the amount of variance due to "
"measurement error. Used to evaluate convergent validity."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Display the heterotrait-monotrait ratio, a measure of the similarity between "
"latent variables, to assess discriminant validity (Henseler et al., 2015). "
"If the HTMT is clearly smaller than one, discriminant validity can be "
"regarded as established."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Display the reliability: the relative amount of test score variance that is "
"explained by the factor(s). Contains coefficient omega (McDonald's) for each "
"indicator group and in total and, if a second-order factor is specified, the "
"omega of the second-order factor. Also provides coefficient alpha "
"(Cronbach's). Note that the total test score variance in the denominator of "
"the reliability equation is the observed test score variance, that is, the "
"summed observed covariance matrix."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid "Display the covariance matrix implied by the model."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Display the covariances between the indicators that remain after taking the "
"model into consideration. A perfect model shows all 0s here."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Display modification indices (MI) above a minimum cutoff. A modification "
"index shows how much the chi-square value of the overall fit would change if "
"the parameter in question were freed up. The expected parameter change (EPC) "
"shows the expected change of the parameter itself."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid "Only modification indices above this value are displayed."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Display the lavaan model syntax that would be needed to run the model in R."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid "Plots of the model fit and the estimated model structure."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Visually show the residual correlations of the indicators, i.e., the "
"correlations that remain unexplained by the model."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid "Graphically show the estimated model structure."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid "Display the parameter estimates on the model plot."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid "Show standardized parameter estimates on the model plot."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid "Font size of the parameter estimates in the model plot."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Show the means (intercepts) in the model plot. Only available when the mean "
"structure is included."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Show the (residual) variances of the indicators and factors in the model "
"plot."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Rotate the model plot by 90 degrees, so that the factors are on the left and "
"the indicators on the right, instead of the factors at the top."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Options for the estimation method, standard errors, missing data handling, "
"and standardization of the parameter estimates."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid "Emulate the results of different software."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Choose the estimation method. The default is ML if only scale variables are "
"used and DWLS if ordinal variables are used. Some estimators set additional "
"options for the test statistic and standard errors in the background. ML-"
"based extensions: MLM (classic robust standard errors, Satorra-Bentler test "
"statistic), MLMV (classic robust standard errors, scaled and shifted test "
"statistic), MLMVS (classic robust standard errors, mean and variance "
"adjusted Satterthwaite-style test statistic), MLF (first-order standard "
"errors, standard test), MLR (Huber-White robust standard errors, Yuan-"
"Bentler T2-star test statistic). Other extensions: WLSM and WLSMV imply DWLS "
"with a scaled or mean and variance adjusted test and robust standard errors, "
"ULSM and ULSMV imply ULS with a scaled or mean and variance adjusted test "
"and robust standard errors. If a method is chosen under Standard errors, it "
"overwrites the standard errors set by the estimator."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"How the standard errors of the parameters are computed. If bootstrap is "
"chosen, the confidence intervals are percentile bootstrap confidence "
"intervals."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid "The number of bootstrap samples used to compute the standard errors."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"The confidence level of the confidence intervals of the parameter estimates."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"How missing values are handled. With ordinal variables only listwise "
"deletion and pairwise are available."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Cases with a missing value on any of the indicators are removed from the "
"analysis."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"The correlations or covariances are computed using all available pairs of "
"observations."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Full-information maximum likelihood uses all available information of every "
"case."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"First, the saturated model is estimated with the EM algorithm; then the "
"model is fitted to the estimated means and covariances."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Same as two-stage, but with standard errors and test statistic that are "
"robust against non-normality."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Display standardized parameter estimates for different standardization "
"schemes."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid "Display the unstandardized parameter estimates."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid "Standardize based on the variances of the latent variables only."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Standardize based on the variances of both the observed and the latent "
"variables."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ConfirmatoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Standardize based on the variances of the observed and the latent variables, "
"excluding exogenous covariates."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ExploratoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid "Number of factors"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ExploratoryFactorAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"The number of factors to extract. To determine this number, use the Number "
"of Factors/Components analysis."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid "Variables"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid "In this box, the variables to perform the analysis on are selected"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid "Data"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid ""
"Specifies whether the data is raw, meaning observations in rows and "
"variables in columns, or whether the data is a variance-covariance matrix. "
"For the latter, the sample size is required."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid "Raw"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid "Variance-covariance matrix"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid "Sample size"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid "Analysis Options"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid "Eigenvalues"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid ""
"Settings for the eigenvalues used by the parallel analysis, the eigenvalue "
"criterion and the scree plot."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid "Method"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid ""
"Whether principal component eigenvalues (PC) or factor eigenvalues (FA) are "
"used for the parallel analysis, the eigenvalue criterion and the scree plot. "
"PC-based eigenvalues are a common choice also when the goal is to determine "
"the number of factors for a factor analysis."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid "Principal components"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid "Factors"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid "Threshold"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid ""
"Threshold for the eigenvalue criterion: factors/components with an "
"eigenvalue above this value are suggested for retention. The default of 1 "
"corresponds to the Kaiser criterion. The eigenvalue type (principal "
"component or factor eigenvalues) follows the method selected above."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid "Parallel Analysis"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid ""
"Parallel analysis compares the eigenvalues of the data to eigenvalues of "
"simulated random data. Factors/components are suggested for retention when "
"their eigenvalue is greater than the 95th percentile of the simulated "
"eigenvalues."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid "Number of iterations"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid ""
"The number of random datasets generated for the parallel analysis. The "
"suggested number is based on the 95th percentile of the simulated "
"eigenvalues, which becomes more stable with more iterations."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid "Correlation Matrix"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid "Which type of correlation matrix the analysis is based on."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid "Pearson"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid "The Pearson correlation matrix is used."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid "Polychoric/tetrachoric"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid ""
"The polychoric/tetrachoric correlation matrix is used. This is sometimes "
"unstable when sample size is small and when some variables do not contain "
"all response categories"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid "Missing Values"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid "Select how to handle missing values."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid "Exclude cases pairwise"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid ""
"If one observation from a variable is missing, all the other variable "
"observations from the same case will still be used for the analysis. In this "
"scenario, it is not necessary to have an observation for all the variables "
"to include the case in the analysis. This option is selected by default."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid "Exclude cases listwise"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid ""
"If one observation from a variable is missing, the whole case, so all the "
"other connected variable observations, will be dismissed from the analysis. "
"In this scenario, observations for every variable are needed to include the "
"case in the analysis. "
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid "Output Options"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid "Parallel analysis table"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid ""
"Displays a table with the real data eigenvalues and the mean eigenvalues of "
"the simulated data. Factors/components suggested for retention are marked "
"with an asterisk."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid "MAP table"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid ""
"Displays a table with the average squared partial correlation after "
"partialling out 0, 1, 2, ... principal components (Velicer's minimum average "
"partial test). The number of components with the lowest value is suggested "
"for retention and marked with an asterisk. This suggestion is always shown "
"in the summary table. It is based on principal components, independent of "
"the method selected under Eigenvalues."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid "Scree plot"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid ""
"Displays a scree plot. The scree plot provides information on how much "
"variance in the data, indicated by the eigenvalue, is explained by each "
"factor/component. The horizontal line marks the eigenvalue threshold."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid "Parallel analysis results"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NumberOfFactors|"
msgid ""
"Display the mean eigenvalues of the simulated data from the parallel "
"analysis in the scree plot."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "PrincipalComponentAnalysis|"
msgid "Number of components"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "PrincipalComponentAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"The number of components to extract. To determine this number, use the "
"Number of Factors/Components analysis."
msgstr ""

#. Shown at the top of the analysis options when a JASP file made with an older version is opened. "Number of Factors/Components" is an analysis name in the Factor menu, translate it the same way there.
msgctxt "Upgrades|"
msgid ""
"Parallel analysis, the eigenvalue criterion, the parallel analysis table and "
"the scree plot have moved to the new <b>Number of Factors/Components</b> "
"analysis in the Factor menu. The number of components is now always entered "
"manually here, so please check that it is still correct."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "Upgrades|"
msgid ""
"This number used to be determined automatically; please check that it is "
"still what you want."
msgstr ""

#. Shown at the top of the analysis options when a JASP file made with an older version is opened. "Number of Factors/Components" is an analysis name in the Factor menu, translate it the same way there.
msgctxt "Upgrades|"
msgid ""
"Parallel analysis, the eigenvalue criterion, the parallel analysis table and "
"the scree plot have moved to the new <b>Number of Factors/Components</b> "
"analysis in the Factor menu. The number of factors is now always entered "
"manually here, so please check that it is still correct."
msgstr ""
